# Real-Time Microsoft Fabric Capacity Command Center

## Project Overview

A real-time monitoring solution designed to track Microsoft Fabric capacity utilization, identify throttling risk, analyze failed operations, and attribute capacity consumption to specific workspaces and Fabric items.

## Business Problem

When Fabric capacity becomes overloaded or throttled, reports, semantic-model queries, pipelines, notebooks, and other operations may slow down or become unavailable.

The objective was to create an operational monitoring experience that answers:

- Is the Fabric capacity currently healthy?
- Is the capacity approaching throttling?
- Which workspace or item is driving utilization?
- Which operations have failed?
- Which Fabric workloads are consuming the most capacity?
- When did the incident occur?
- What recovery action should be taken?

## Solution Architecture

Fabric Capacity Events -> Real-Time Hub -> Eventstream -> Eventhouse / KQL Database -> KQL Transformation and Analytics Layer -> Fabric Real-Time Dashboard -> Alerts and Recovery Architecture

